# A chip the system offers no frame interpolator to (DM_TEST_NO_FG=1; Apple lists it from the M1 on, so this is the fallback nobody should need): the conventional picture at the real frame rate, with no row to change it.
# With interpolators (every Mac so far) it's video_fg_mac.scn
name video_no_fg_mac
requires mac-app
# In front: without frame generation the Mac presents straight into the window, and a background run's window sits outside every screen, where the
# system sometimes holds its images back: the GPU then waits on them, the game stops in its present wait and a quit can't save (2 of 20 runs in
# the background on 2026-11-07, 0 of 20 in front; dm/verify/debugging.md)
front visibility
save warlock
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1 DM_TEST_NO_FG=1
timeout 200

enter_game
sleep 6
system_quit
check event picture how=first up=1 fg=0
check log_has "frame interpolator supported: no"
check no_event mfx who=temporal op=build
check no_red
check no_red_log
